traceability.evidence:
Story file exists and is a concrete spec: docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md (7,150 bytes).,Rule implementation updated to support JSDoc coexistence:
  - src/rules/helpers/valid-annotation-format-internal.ts:
    - normalizeCommentLine(rawLine: string): preserves line boundaries, strips leading '*' but only anchors on @story/@req/@supports, leaving other JSDoc tags intact for later detection.
    - isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine(normalized: string):
      ```ts
      export function isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine(normalized: string): boolean {
        const trimmed = normalized.trimStart();
        if (!trimmed || !trimmed.startsWith("@")) {
          return false;
        }

        if (/^@(story|req|supports)\b/.test(trimmed)) {
          return false;
        }

        return true;
      }
      ```
      This matches the story’s boundary-detection requirement (treat any `@tag` line that is not @story/@req/@supports as a boundary) and is annotated with:
      `@supports docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md` and `@req REQ-JSDOC-BOUNDARY-DETECTION`, `@req REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE`.,Rule line-processing logic enforces termination, continuation, and JSDoc-boundary behavior:
  - src/rules/valid-annotation-format.ts (processCommentLine):
    ```ts
    function processCommentLine({ normalized, pending, context, comment, options }): PendingAnnotation | null {
      if (!normalized) {
        return pending;
      }

      const isStory = /@story\b/.test(normalized);
      const isReq = /@req\b/.test(normalized);
      const isImplements = /@supports\b/.test(normalized);

      if (isImplements) {
        const implementsValue = normalized.replace(/^@supports\b/, "").trim();
        validateImplementsAnnotation(context, comment, implementsValue, options);
        return pending;
      }

      if (isStory || isReq) {
        finalizePendingAnnotation(context, comment, options, pending);
        const value = normalized.replace(/^@story\b|^@req\b/, "").trim();
        return {
          type: isStory ? "story" : "req",
          value,
          hasValue: value.trim().length > 0,
        };
      }

      // JSDoc tag coexistence behavior
      // @supports docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC
      if (isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine(normalized)) {
        finalizePendingAnnotation(context, comment, options, pending);
        return null;
      }

      if (pending) {
        const continuation = normalized.trim();
        if (!continuation) {
          return pending;
        }
        const updatedValue = pending.value
          ? `${pending.value} ${continuation}`
          : continuation;
        return {
          ...pending,
          value: updatedValue,
          hasValue: pending.hasValue || continuation.length > 0,
        };
      }

      return pending;
    }
    ```
    This directly implements:
    - REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION (boundary terminates value when next line is a JSDoc tag),
    - REQ-JSDOC-BOUNDARY-DETECTION (uses isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine),
    - REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC (only non-`@tag` lines are treated as continuations),
    and is annotated with `@supports docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md` in the JSDoc.,Tests explicitly tied to this story verify the JSDoc coexistence scenarios:
